3. DOUBLE OR NOTHING (one hand, the dealer STANDS ON ALL 17s, ties on 19/20 win, other ties dealt again; win pays exactly 2x)
Win chance per resolved hand p = 0.50045487064506489 (best play) · RTP best play 100.0910% (= 2p) · basic strategy 100.0721% · worst play 92.0888% · always stand 94.7814% · always hit 97.3050% · 1.0422 deals per resolved hand.
Play                              RTP  Win chance  Push / deal  Deals / hand  RTP, dealer hits S17
Best play                   100.0910%    50.0455%       4.052%       1.04223              99.9077%
Basic strategy (conv. chart)  100.0721%    50.0360%       4.000%       1.04166              99.8981%
Worst play                   92.0888%    46.0444%       3.683%       1.03824              91.9174%
Always stand                 94.7814%    47.3907%       3.145%       1.03247              94.8811%
Always hit                   97.3050%    48.6525%       4.541%       1.04757              96.8500%
Basic strategy = the CR's "ordinary blackjack basic strategy" = the conventional no-doubling chart (strategy.js convMask: hard 12 stand against 4-6 else hit; hard 13-16 stand against 2-6 else hit; soft 17 hit; soft 18 stand against 2-8, hit against 9, 10, A); it reproduces the CR's 99.8981% (dealer hits soft 17) and 100.0721% (stands). The rules sheet's own basic play (a board strategy; soft 18 = stand) applied to this hand returns 99.9579%.
Base game and DOUBLE OR NOTHING: no rounding (exact cents at every legal bet). Minimum $0.02 for DOUBLE OR NOTHING / DOUBLE HALF; DOUBLE HALF doubles half (floor of the cents) and banks the rest.

4. RUN-BAR POLICIES (one bet per round, runs funded by the round's winnings; best play on the board and in DOUBLE OR NOTHING)
P0 cash out · P2 DOUBLE OR NOTHING once · P3 DOUBLE OR NOTHING while offered (to the 1,000x cap / max win) · P4 uniform random pick among the buttons shown (CASH OUT / DOUBLE OR NOTHING / DOUBLE HALF) at every bar · P5 DOUBLE HALF once
(P1, RUN IT AGAIN once, is retired. Since the dealer stands on all 17s a double returns MORE than 100%, so cashing out (P0) no longer bounds the policies: P2 P3 P4 P5 all beat P0. The best any policy can do is section 7.) P4 simulation rows are the first-pass seeds.
Policy    Exact $1  Exact $10 Exact $100   SD $10  Hit $10   Simulation $10 (95% CI)              Simulation $100 (95% CI)
P0        94.3679%   94.3679%   94.3679%    0.942   69.53%   94.302% [93.890%, 94.714%]           94.265% [93.683%, 94.847%]
P2        94.4538%   94.4538%   94.4538%    1.633   34.80%   95.019% [94.302%, 95.735%]           95.142% [94.133%, 96.152%]
P3        95.2299%   95.2299%   95.2299%   42.842    0.07%   86.170% [68.700%, 103.639%]          95.027% [67.776%, 122.278%]
P4        94.4825%   94.4825%   94.4825%   2.692*  49.68%*   94.069% [93.291%, 94.848%]           93.775% [92.423%, 95.127%]
P5        94.4108%   94.4108%   94.4108%    1.154   69.53%   94.213% [93.708%, 94.718%]           94.395% [93.683%, 95.107%]
* P4: the exact SD and hit rate use the cut paths valued by the tail model (SD a lower bound, hit rate an upper bound, both by the cut mass below).
P5 closed form (DOUBLE HALF once): E[pay] = a + (2w - 1) x half for a first win of a cents (half = floor(a/2) >= 2 cents), w = 0.500455, 2w - 1 = 0.000910; RTP(P5) - RTP(P0) = $1 0.04293 pts, $10 0.04293 pts, $100 0.04293 pts; the bar model equals the closed form to 1e-12 at every bet; hit rate = the board hit rate.
P4 at $1 (small amounts, minimum $0.02): exact 94.4825% (cut mass 0.0184%); simulation 200,000 rounds 95.163% [93.777%, 96.550%] (crypto 1401, 1402; picks 4411, 4412): exact inside; hit rate 49.53% [49.31%, 49.75%] v exact 49.68%: inside.
P5 at $1 (small amounts, minimum $0.02): exact 94.4108%; simulation 200,000 rounds 94.222% [93.712%, 94.733%] (crypto 1501, 1502): exact inside; hit rate 69.38% [69.18%, 69.58%] v exact 69.53%: inside.
P4 exact: full recursion of every rule, cut at path probability 1e-12; cut mass 0.0184% at $1, 0.0188% at $10, 0.0188% at $100; cut paths valued by a linear tail model (alpha 1.000607 x RUN BANK + beta 1.001214 x held; an estimate). Bracket at $10 (cut paths at 0 / at Lambda x their total, Lambda = the bound on V*/(S+B) over all states from the bar optimum, 1.073): [94.1888%, 94.5034%]; at $1 [94.1887%, 94.5001%]; at $100 [94.1888%, 94.5068%]. The old upper bound (a cut path is worth at most its total) is invalid now that a double returns more than 100%; the upper end is only as good as the power-law extension of the solved ammo. Convergence of the cut: out/exact_runs_convergence.log.

